ared with conventional treatment and risk of complications in patients with Type 2 diabetes. Lancet. 1998;352:837&#x02013;51. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9742976</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR4"><label>4.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>UKPDS Group</collab></person-group><article-title>UKPDS 34: Effect of intensive blood-glucose control with metformin on complications on overweight patients with type 2 diabetes</article-title><source>Lancet</source><year>1998</year><volume>352</volume><fpage>854</fpage><lpage>865</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0140-6736(05)61359-1</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">UKPDS Group. UKPDS 34: Effect of intensive blood-glucose control with metformin on complications on overweight patients with type 2 diabetes. Lancet. 1998;352:854&#x02013;65. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9742977</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR5"><label>5.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Boccuzzi</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Wogen</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Fox</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Sung</surname><given-names>JCY</given-names></name><name><surname>Shah</surname><given-names>AB</given-names></name><name><surname>Kim</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Utilization of oral antihyperglycemic agents in a drug-insured US population</article-title><source>Diabetes Care</source><year>2001</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>1411</fpage><lpage>1415</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2337/diacare.24.8.1411</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Boccuzzi SJ, Wogen J, Fox J, Sung JCY, Shah AB, Kim J. Utilization of oral antihyperglycemic agents in a drug-insured US population. Diabetes Care. 2001;24:1411&#x02013;15. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11473078</pub